    {
      "id": "20941bb8-957c-4375-918b-42f47a20ac5e",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        576,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Get the number of new & lost backlinks with DataForSEO and save the data to the spreadsheet\nCreate a DataForSEO connection.\nSelect the same spreadsheet with your targets as in the first Google Sheets node."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b5ccfcef-35b6-44e6-b98c-6dc5db0042a8",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -672,
        -144
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 592,
        "height": 976,
        "content": "This workflow runs a bulk backlink analysis across five DataForSEO endpoints from a single Google Sheet, with each endpoint having its own branch.\nThe workflow is modular: connect the branches that match the backlinks data you need, leave the rest disconnected, and run it. You can use one branch, several, or all five in the same execution.\n\n## Available branches\n\n - Bulk Backlinks: live backlink counts for up to 1000 targets.\n - Bulk New & Lost Backlinks: newly acquired and recently lost backlinks per target.\n - Bulk Referring Domains: live referring domain counts, including nofollow and main domain counts.\n - Bulk New & Lost Referring Domains: newly acquired and recently lost referring domains per target.\n - Bulk Spam Scores: DataForSEO Spam Score (0-100) for each target.\n\n## How it works\n\n - Triggers manually.\n - Reads target domains from your Google Sheet through the shared Get targets node.\n - Aggregates the domains into a single batch request.\n - Routes the batch through each connected DataForSEO endpoint branch.\n - Splits the response and writes the results back into the Google Sheet, one branch per column group.\n\n## Setup steps\n\n - Create or select your DataForSEO connection (use your [API login and password](https://app.dataforseo.com/api-access)).\n - Create or select your Google Sheets connection.\n - Prepare your Google Sheet with target domains following the required column structure.\n - Select the same spreadsheet in the Get targets node and in every\n - Update rows in the sheet node you plan to use.\n - Keep only the endpoint branches you want to run and disconnect the rest.\n - Run the workflow.\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
